// error
// #3449, epic #2185: a CONSTANT-FOLDED BINARY receiver still passed `bit
// check` silently even after #3444 taught `vDeclRooted` to trust a bare
// literal receiver (`1.5.zzz`, `"a".zzz`, `(5).zzz`). `1.5 + 1.0` is a
// `Tag.Binary` node — neither a literal tag nor one of the chained-receiver
// tags (`Member`/`Index`/`Call`/`TryExpr`) — so it fell through to
// `vDeclRooted`'s final `return false` and `vMember` bailed out before
// validating the member. `bit build` then refused at lowering with the
// spanless E0092 "cannot lower a call whose callee does not resolve to a
// function" — the same #2185 shape every other case in this family hit
// before its own fix landed.
fn main() {
  let y = (1.5 + 1.0).zzz
  println("${y}")
}
